1227	## Knowledge Accumulation Schema
1228	
1229	### `src/schema/knowledge.ts` — Insight and KnowledgeStore schemas
1230	
1231	Zod schemas and inferred TypeScript types for the knowledge accumulation system. All types are inferred via `z.infer<>` — no handwritten duplicate interfaces.
1232	
1233	```typescript
1234	// Regex for valid project slugs: must start with an alphanumeric character, followed by
1235	// letters, digits, underscores, or hyphens only. Rejects '/', '\\', '.', spaces, and any
1236	// character that could escape the .knowledge/ directory.
1237	// Single source of truth — used by both InsightSchema.project_slug Zod refinement and
1238	// KnowledgeStoreManager._validateSlug(). Update this constant to change the slug policy
1239	// in both places simultaneously.
1240	export const PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX: RegExp; // /^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*$/
1241	
1242	// Scope enum: 'global' (applies across all projects) | 'project' (scoped to a specific project).
1243	// Note: when scope === 'project', project_slug must be present. This constraint is enforced
1244	// by the storage layer (KnowledgeStoreManager), not by this schema, so the schema remains
1245	// composable and usable without runtime context.
1246	const InsightScope: z.ZodEnum<['global', 'project']>;
1247	type InsightScope = 'global' | 'project';
1248	
1249	// Single reusable knowledge record stored in the knowledge base.
1250	// Optional fields: project_slug (required by storage layer when scope === 'project'),
1251	// updated_at (set when an insight is amended after initial creation),
1252	// superseded_by (id of the insight that replaces this one — no referential integrity enforced at schema layer).
1253	// confidence: 0–1 float; no range constraint enforced — forward-looking field.
1254	const InsightSchema: z.ZodObject<{
1255	  id: z.ZodNumber;              // integer; storage layer should enforce id >= 1; per-store only — not globally unique across global and project stores
1256	  scope: typeof InsightScope;
1257	  project_slug: z.ZodOptional<z.ZodString>;
1258	  title: z.ZodString;
1259	  content: z.ZodString;
1260	  category: z.ZodString;
1261	  tags: z.ZodArray<z.ZodString>;
1262	  source: z.ZodString;
1263	  created_at: z.ZodString;      // ISO 8601 timestamp
1264	  updated_at: z.ZodOptional<z.ZodString>;
1265	  confidence: z.ZodNumber;      // 0–1 float; no range enforced at schema layer
1266	  superseded_by: z.ZodOptional<z.ZodNumber>; // integer id of superseding insight
1267	}>;
1268	type Insight = z.infer<typeof InsightSchema>;
1269	
1270	// Top-level structure for .knowledge/store.json.
1271	// - version: schema version string (e.g. "1.0.0") for forward-compatibility
1272	// - last_updated: ISO 8601 timestamp of the most recent write
1273	// - next_id: auto-increment counter; assigned to the next insight added
1274	// - insights: flat array of all stored Insight records
1275	const KnowledgeStoreSchema: z.ZodObject<{
1276	  version: z.ZodString;
1277	  last_updated: z.ZodString;
1278	  next_id: z.ZodNumber;         // nonnegative integer
1279	  insights: z.ZodArray<typeof InsightSchema>;
1280	}>;
1281	type KnowledgeStore = z.infer<typeof KnowledgeStoreSchema>;
1282	```
1283	
1284	**Design notes:**
1285	- `scope === 'project'` → `project_slug` required constraint is owned by the storage layer (`KnowledgeStoreManager`, WP-002+), not this schema. The schema accepts `project_slug` as optional to remain context-free and composable.
1286	- Storage layer should enforce `z.number().int().positive()` for `id` (schema accepts 0) and `z.number().finite()` for `confidence` (schema accepts `Infinity`) when persisting.
1287	- Empty strings for `title`, `content`, `source`, `category` are accepted by the schema; storage layer should guard against them.
